# Theme Token Ownership: Core vs Module

## Rule

Module-specific CSS custom properties (`--theme-*` and `--color-*`) must NEVER be defined in the core theme files or `bifrost.scss`. They must be defined in the module's own SCSS file.

The bifrost core must have no knowledge of module-specific tokens. This mirrors the architectural restriction applied to components.

## Core theme files (ONLY generic tokens)

- `studio/src/bifrost/styles/theme.light.scss` — light tokens for shared UI surfaces
- `studio/src/bifrost/styles/theme.dark.scss` — dark tokens for shared UI surfaces
- `studio/src/bifrost/styles/bifrost.scss` — structural layout + overrides using core tokens

These files must only contain tokens that apply to the Studio's shared UI (activity bar, editor tabs, pane, tree view, buttons, inputs, tables, modals, notifications, etc.).

## Module SCSS files (module-specific tokens)

Each module defines its own theme tokens in its SCSS file using the explicit class pattern:

```scss
.bifrost.bifrost-theme--light {
  --theme-my-module-bg: #fff;
}

.bifrost.bifrost-theme--dark {
  --theme-my-module-bg: #323232;
}
```

Themed CSS overrides for third-party library elements (e.g., bpmn-js `.djs-palette`, `.bjs-container`) also belong in the module that imports and uses that library, not in `bifrost.scss`.

## Current token ownership

| Module | Token prefixes | SCSS file |
|-----------|---------------|-----------|
| `bpmn-editor` | `--theme-diagram-*`, `--theme-color-picker-*` | `bpmn-editor/styles/bpmn.scss` |
| `bpmn-diff` | `--theme-diff-*` | `bpmn-diff/styles/component.bpmn-diff.scss` |
| `engine-debugger` | `--color-engine__debugger-*`, `--color-flow-node-*` | `engine-debugger/EngineDebugger.scss` |
| `engine-browser` | `--color-engine__browser-*` | `engine-browser/EngineBrowser.scss` |
| `engine-bpmn-viewer` | `--color-engine__bpmn-viewer-*` | `engine-bpmn-viewer/RemoteBpmnViewer.scss` |

## Alias variable scope

Theme-dependent alias variables (`--color-*: var(--theme-*)`) must be defined inside `.bifrost { }`, never on `:root`. Only fixed color values (e.g., `--color-black: #000`) belong on `:root`.

## When adding new tokens

1. If the token is used across multiple shared components — add to `theme.light.scss` and `theme.dark.scss`
2. If the token is used by a single module — add to that module.s SCSS file
3. ALWAYS provide both light and dark values using `.bifrost.bifrost-theme--light` and `.bifrost.bifrost-theme--dark` selectors
